  "questions": [
    {
      "key": "fa911c21-ddcf-4404-a81a-08edaf716778",
      "id": "Q-01",
      "text": "Does optical zoom (1x against 5x) on the varifocal cameras change the first-cue, confirmed and identified ranges for the same Mavic 3 approach, and by how much against the run-to-run variation?",
      "note": "Response: first possible, confirmed and identified range per camera per run; the difference between levels and the spread within a level. Vary: optical zoom on CAM-3 and CAM-4 (1x, 5x). Hold: CAM-1 and CAM-2 at 80 deg, 40 m AGL, 8 m/s, head-on, same path. Record: sun, sky background, wind. Replicates: 3 runs per level, levels alternated. Target-absent interval: 120 s before launch. A second factor, defined background condition, can replace zoom with the same profile."
    }
  ],
